                        "sense_id": "1c41db61-bddf-3986-b092-47c004bcb82e",
                        "entry_id": "849b6fd9-bd74-3894-b361-020c129531e7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relating to, or resembling, the butterflies of the family Pieridae."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8d0ae3b-3763-423f-ba61-13645ba8d607",
                                "sense_id": "1c41db61-bddf-3986-b092-47c004bcb82e",
                                "text": "The bearing of the geographical distribution of existing Pierine forms upon the preceding phylogenetic conclusions was then considered, and it was shown that the facts of distribution, taken in connection with what was known of the means of transit possible for insects, and especially of the migratory habits of certain Pierines, were in general accordance with the same conclusions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9848dae3-0548-4783-94ff-bd1aea96c08d",
                                "sense_id": "1c41db61-bddf-3986-b092-47c004bcb82e",
                                "text": "No pigment of similar constitution to the Pierine white, yellow, and red, was found by Mr. Hopkins in any other butterfly—not even in the allied Papilioninae."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60df4e00-1862-4ec9-9b50-1008e8cfa348",
                                "sense_id": "1c41db61-bddf-3986-b092-47c004bcb82e",
                                "text": "Perhaps some of the most interesting data on such properties of adaptive response, and constraints upon it, come from the recent studies of Shapiro on Andean pierine butterflies."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
