                    {
                        "sense_id": "42c46709-8fbf-35f6-b2a6-a2cec867c1cf",
                        "entry_id": "588e5ca0-c163-3f74-a0ee-edda5e5100e8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A butterfly of the family Pieridae."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4f1c7ce-70ee-44ba-8cb7-4fbe469925b8",
                                "sense_id": "42c46709-8fbf-35f6-b2a6-a2cec867c1cf",
                                "text": "Rather than reviewing the physics and physiology of butterfly thermoregulation here, I will simply note that thermoregulatory advantage is not yet proven for the seasonal phenotypes of any pierine, though strongly suspected; increased survivorship […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "00b56f59-60d2-4413-9e18-d0e4d87c638d",
                                "sense_id": "42c46709-8fbf-35f6-b2a6-a2cec867c1cf",
                                "text": "Any hope that the pierines would help to define “the level at which r-K phenomena should be sought has been dashed: apparently species groups (or subgenera, or splitters' genera) are r- or K-selected in the holarctic, whereas in Tatochila the same amount of differentiation is found among populations in a complex in which the process of speciation has not yet been completed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47a38fda-9e26-4a8b-bb53-0ac6baf3499a",
                                "sense_id": "42c46709-8fbf-35f6-b2a6-a2cec867c1cf",
                                "text": "For Africa, Marshall has collected some fortysix observations of which almost half are concerned with Pierines."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
